No-teleport means that you cannot teleport yourself, nor can monsters
teleport away as they normally can.

You *can* teleport others and you can teleport items, though. Also,
monsters that teleport to the stairs to heal up can still do that on those
levels (which I find illogical, but assumedly necessary for game balance).

The first no-teleport zone you'll usually find is Sokoban.

For example, on Sokoban, you cannot teleport yourself, nymphs cannot
teleport away, but you *can* use a wand of teleportation to move a boulder
or temporarily get rid of a nymph.

